OL,3,AArrest made after fire at Hitler's
OL,4,AEagle's Nest retreat
OL,5,
OL,6,FPolice in the south German state of
OL,7,FBavaria have detained a suspect during
OL,8,Fa fire at Adolf Hitler's Alpine
OL,9,Fmountain retreat, the Kehlsteinhaus,
OL,10,Falso known as the Eagle's Nest.
OL,12,FDispatchers in Traunstein received a
OL,13,Ffire alarm from the building at 21:15
OL,14,F(19:15 GMT) on Friday, and firefighters
OL,15,Ffound it engulfed in flames.
OL,17,FDifficult terrain was hindering efforts
OL,18,Fto extinguish the blaze and it was
OL,19,Fstill burning early on Saturday, police
OL,20,Fsaid, with some 200 emergency personnel
OL,21,Fdeployed. There were no reports of
OL,22,Finjuries.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,0,100
